// Families 9 and 10 of the catalogue (docs/ridonculous-race-scenes.md §9, §10): body, fear and
// limits (injury, illness, exhaustion, gross-out, phobia, quit-talk, delayed-reaction), and the place
// itself (arrival-awe, identity-moment, cultural-task, souvenir, identity-crisis, weather). Written to
// docs/rr-writers-brief.md.
// Who is who: a and b are the team. a is the one it happens to (hurt, sick, scared, wanting to quit);
// for weather and souvenir a is the team's leader. Injuries are never gory and never mocked; fear is
// real. aElder gates the parent lines (true: a is the parent; false: b is).
// What the engine does not keep, and how the lines live with it:
//   - which body part, which illness, which fear, which weather, which souvenir: each entry sets its
//     own in a beat or its first line, and general entries stay with "it" and "this";
//   - a phobia's object is only the task's type, so specific fears are gated on taskType and the
//     general entries talk about being scared, not of what;
//   - places are gated on the four place ids; everything else stays setting-neutral;
//   - in-their-element can fire (rarely) on a task the identity is not good at, so its identity
//     hook turns are gated on idGood and a plain confident line covers the rest.
